One of the best (if not the best) Worms classic games! There's little to add to it, as it's considered a masterpiece!
-Highly customisable matches, solo AND multiplayer (and with maps you can create using a built-in tool or some advanced free programs in the community);
-Huge arsenal of weapons (even compared to modern Worms games);
-Online Multiplayer (Yes! There're people still playing this 1999's game online. It's that good!);

-Local Multiplayer with up to 6 teams and 48 worms (Thanks to the 2010 upgrade);
-33 solo missions that will gradually test your skills;
-A Training session that can help you a lot;
-A Deathmatch mode to entertain good players and make the hardened ones try to finish it;
-Extras and Rewards that are given to you as you complete trainnings and missions (and can be easily unlocked with mods, if you wish);
-Many, many, many Addons and Mods from years of community;
-Many (new) graphic options to suite your pc configuration (but it doesn't replace the classic art style);
The game received a big upgrade in 2010, is updated from time to time, and can run in all machines (Windows, Linux and Macs). If a problem occur (which in unusual) you just need a quick look on google to find a solution.
I've spent more than 50 hours playing it solo and as local coop. If you think my opinion is spoiled by nostalgia, I must mention that I've only got my own copy in mid 2013 and barely played this game when I was young.
If you are still not sure, buy it on sale or consult a doctor.

One of the classics of my childhood.
Ideal party game:
- local coop with one PC (best if you can play it on a big screen TV);
- fun, easy-to-pick-up gameplay;
- random and balanced enough in the end (especially with more than 2 players);
- ideal length (guaranteed to end soon after started with heated arguments).
I really liked the extent of customization available - just make sure not to waste too much time on creating teams or maps!
Recommend picking it up on a sale!

How to git gut at r6siege:
1. Use your teamchat to only yell at people's mistakes, preferably in russian;
2. Play with as much ping as possible, that way you see people and can kill them after they're already gone, plus you and your fellas can go eat something while waiting for the round to start;
3. Turn your fov to 90 to only later find out that it's vertical and that's the reason for your innability to see enemies;
4. Play this game without headphones and while listening to music, it's very effective;
5. When you're the last man alive on your team, run away and save your weapon for the next round.
11/9, would love to get killed by a guy who I never saw because of his ping again.

