I usually don't make rewiews on steam, but this one title really deserve someone being honest and rewiew it as honestly as possible;
I can't say the game is bad, it is actually funny and till a degree "playable", BUT... what i'm talking about is the game PLUS MODS, if you ever seen the game trought youtube, you didn't seen the REAL GAME, but a game so incomplete, that requires  dozens of mods for be able to do the most basic things you'd want from a city builder game (believe it or not, it miss things Sim City 2013 has...) some example being:
Tourism: you can build up to 25 tiles of city, but still be able to get max 20 weekly tourists... guys even made a New york city like city, but with few to no tourists at all; The thing become sad when you build airports and civil ports, and there start coming empty airplanes and cruisers-like ships.
Decorations: In a game, where you can reach max population (cpu permetting) just spamming residential and offices zones with x3 speed, the funny part is surely not the challenge, but making your city as beauty as possible, or even as realistic as possible... well, this game is not the case, with decorations the game means  parks, and there are like 6 parks, 2(with a european theme map, if not just 1) sport parks, a tiny basketball and a tiny tennis park, 3 plazes and just 2 kind of pedestrians routes (gravel and rock);
If you search realism, the game will surprise you, letting you build like in dwarf fortress, but without the y-z lines (aka just in a plane), yes, you can make highways or even bridges, but all with stupid self imponed restrictions like:
you can't build a tunnel going under a mountain if it isn't going up or down (like saying making the 90% of existing tunnels in the world is impossible);
you can't make 2 curved roads encounter near every time, because of restrictions again;
you can't make roads going under the actual plain level, without making it a underground tunnel;
There aren't angled housed,(like if you wanna make 2 roads encounter forming an angle different from 90°/270° there will be no houses, shops, offices, industries or whatever building shaped good enough to be able to be built in a different angle than the two said up).
From what i'm writing, it can appear i want too much from a game, and the missing things, are just little things, and thus, you wouldn't need them near every time, but try see your real life city on google maps or any map, and try make it in game, nothing other than the squares built quartiers will be possible to be built in game, and no, i'm not talking about a city like the greatest ones, where there are thousand of strange shaped roads and buildings, but i'm talking about little to middle sized cities, where originality is not the key word for build them.
Concluding it, i have to say that i have nothing against mods and modders themselves, but in order to have a full game, you have to activate dozens of mods and houndred (if not thousands) of assets; now a decent enough pc, can manage the double size of the game and all the mods/assests, but being they made by the community, stability is not ever contemplated, and every update you have to wait modders to update (if they do) your essential mods in order to play a $30 paid game, No thanks!

