-Nominated to "Test of Time Steam Award"-
I first played this game when it was launched in 2004-yes, 12 years ago; and when finally an English version was released on Steam, I didn't even hesitate to buy it, and replayed it all the way through. Even after 12 years this game didn't fail to deliver a satisfying experience. It might be nostalgia at work, but surprisingly the game didn't feel as dated as I imagined it'd be. I'd recommand this game to anyone who enjoys RPG, especially one with a rich storyline and thorough chracter development. This is one of those games that after you finish it you just wouldn't stop thinking about it. The downside is that the characters can appear "too sterotypical and predictable"; however somehow they still managed to grow on me, and the female protagnoist Estelle has become one of my favourtie JRPG charaters.
TL;DR- If you like JRPG, this is a must have;
if you don't know what JRPG is but enjoy games with storyline, try it;
If you don't care much about stories and hate reading bunch of dialogues, perhaps this game isn't for you.

